# Styling & Colors

## Color Palette (CSS Variables in custom.css)

| Token | Value | Usage |
|-------|-------|-------|
| `--color-footer-bg` | `#efefef` | `.footer` bar, `theme-color` meta |
| `--color-link` | `red` | `.legal-content a:link` |
| `--color-link-visited` | `green` | `.legal-content a:visited` |
| UIkit defaults | — | Cards, navbar, offcanvas on all pages |

Do not change these color values. Homepage card links inherit UIkit defaults.

## Design Tokens

`custom.css` defines shared tokens in `:root`:

- **Typography:** `--font-sans`, `--text-xs` through `--text-2xl` (fluid `clamp()` scale)
- **Spacing:** `--space-xs` through `--space-2xl`
- **Layout:** `--content-max` (68rem), `--content-narrow` (42rem), `--content-reading` (38rem)
- **Effects:** `--radius-sm/md/lg`, `--shadow-sm/md/lg`, `--transition-fast/base`

Use these tokens for new styles; avoid hard-coded pixel values.

## Typography

- **System font stack:** `system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, ...`
- **Hero title:** `.site-hero .site-title` — larger clamp scale
- **Card titles:** `h2.uk-card-title` at `--text-xl`
- **Card body:** `.card-description` (primary text), `.card-meta` (muted, `--text-xs`)
- **Legal headings:** `h2` section titles, `h3` subsections

## CSS Organization

| Location | Scope |
|----------|-------|
| `custom.css` | All active pages — tokens, skip link, layout shell, navbar, hero, persona cards, footer, legal |

## Responsive Breakpoints

- **960px:** Wider container padding, hero/card spacing
- **UIkit grid:** `@m` suffix (`uk-child-width-1-3@m`) — 3 columns from medium breakpoint up

## Accessibility

- Skip link: `.skip-link` (visible on focus)
- Reduced motion: `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` disables hover transforms
- Focus: `:focus-visible` outline on interactive elements

## Do Not

- Change the color palette (`#efefef`, `red`, `green`)
- Introduce CSS preprocessors, Tailwind, or a second component library without explicit request
- Break the light, minimal aesthetic with heavy gradients or dark themes
